WEBVTT

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.650
Starting outermost...

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.150
Neptune, Uranus, Saturn.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:58.790
Jupiter, Mars, Earth, Venus, Mercury.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.710
And I am on the Sun.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.660
If you can pass these orbiting planets

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.670
and make your way to the Sun, you win.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.730
The planets will start
to rotate in set courses

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.850
along their respective orbits.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.330
But be careful.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:34.460
Once the time limit is reached...

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.370
Like a wooden cross... puzzle.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.360
Yes. And this Sun is the same.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.380
When you step on the Sun's ring...

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.170
The Sun will crumble.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.540
I will fall....

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.010
...and die.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.730
Then, I will be eternal inside you.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.720
Rook...

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.690
A puzzle that if Kaito solves,
Rook is sure to die, huh?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.060
But that's... a puzzle
like that is WEIRD!

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.130
Those two are friends!

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.200
They can't do a puzzle like that! Kaito...

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.290
You can't escape.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:29.210
You know that,
don't you, Kaito?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.140
I got no intention of tryin'.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:36.310
A puzzle with the movement
of the planets as a motif, huh?

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.920
That's pretty awesome.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.590
But. It was made just for killin' people.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.610
So it's a no-good, piece-of-crap puzzle!

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.280
Master Rook. What have you done?!

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.520
What's this mean?!

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.920
The puzzle has become simple.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.140
Unbelievably so.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.620
Now, even you could solve it.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.800
How about THIS?

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.510
We can't have you waste time on some

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.040
"piece-of-crap puzzle."

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.120
Fine. I'll solve it.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.770
I'll solve your
piece-of-crap puzzle,

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.270
get the Book of God, and then burn it!

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.530
But, Rook, I'm definitely gonna save you!

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.020
That's a puzzle I WILL solve!

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:48.500
This puzzle has only
one solution: Kill me.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.410
How do you intend to find another answer?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.420
You know...

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.590
I'll think of that right now!

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.110
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.820
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.620
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.410
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.160
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:35.670
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:40.380
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.590
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.260
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.260
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.560
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.520
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.310
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.860
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.110
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.780
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.030
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.370
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.000
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.880
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.550
Brain diver

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.300
Brain diver

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.940
Let's Begin Puzzle Time!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.840
Solve the puzzle AND save Rook?

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.710
Even for the great Kaito Daimon,

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.400
it will be impossible
to find another solution

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.800
to this puzzle, now that it's become

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.810
so easy.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.600
Also, Kaito has rejected the
Armlet of Orpheus.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.420
This will be a tough fight.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.990
More so than any puzzle up till now.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.300
H-He'll be fine.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.710
Even without the Armlet,

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.960
Kaito was able to save Gammon.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.420
He'll do it this time, too!

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:38.860
Let's hope so.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.430
Gammon!

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.130
Hey. It's been a while.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.380
What are you doing here, you traitor?!

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.350
That ain't nice.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:51.250
And after I rescued
this hostage here.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.640
The principal!

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.720
I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.000
So, Gammon, you DIDN'T betray us?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.300
Has the puzzle already started?

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.060
The heck is that?

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.890
If he solves the puzzle, Rook dies, huh?

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:14.290
Release through being
killed by a friend...

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:17.330
What a sad and brutal puzzle.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:22.760
However, we must watch it to its climax.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.340
No matter what happens.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:28.880
That is the responsibility of we

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.440
who have led them to this point.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.550
Can you solve this puzzle, Dumbass?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.100
Kaito Daimon...

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.900
There's no time for dilly-dallyin'.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.650
I have to save Rook and get

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.410
the two of us out of this puzzle.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.730
That is MY puzzle.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.410
And I'm gonna solve it!

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.900
When Rook was eating takoyaki,

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:01.430
or at the coffee shop,

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:03.430
or at the bookstore, he smiled.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.790
He was smiling!

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:09.050
No way can I let that smiling face die!

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.370
Kaito is getting close to Rook.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.190
There's no other way.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.150
But at this rate...

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.940
Nothing else can be done.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.020
No way!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.130
I, Ana, and all of us must believe.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.570
In the light. In the future.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.190
He's reached Mars.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.160
Four more till the Sun.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.090
Kaito...

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.700
Just as Rook planned it, huh?

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.220
In any case, I gotta keep going.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.020
Two more.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:09.470
Nonoha!

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.150
Dammit!

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:23.690
I feel it.

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:27.290
This puzzle wants me to solve it.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.440
So, there MUST be an answer.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.800
Think. Think, dammit!

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.070
You've arrived, Kaito.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:55.320
The answer...

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:57.580
I can't see the answer!

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.560
He got on it. The last planet.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.420
If he jumps from that
onto the Sun's ring...

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.960
The puzzle will be done.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.180
Come, Kaito. Make me eternal.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.250
Then those pleasant days
will loop inside you.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.530
Just the two of us.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.680
For eternity.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:26.980
Rook.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:34.890
Kaito!

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.110
Kaito has... stopped moving.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.450
He's approaching Phi-Brain potential,

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.990
even without the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:45.430
Right now, Kaito can't
even hear our voices.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.900
It was Rook who made this puzzle.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.250
WHY did he make this puzzle?

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.010
Planets... Wooden cross puzzles...

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.350
That...

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:09.430
It's the same as this!

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:14.250
But why? Is it a trap?

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:17.650
No, I believe.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.070
Rook wouldn't use this for a trap.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.750
But this ain't enough
to solve the puzzle.

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.960
Oh! Those guys...

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:39.610
Nonoha!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.050
When this puzzle's done with,

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.720
will you make one for me?

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:50.060
A Nonoha Sweets Birthday Special?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.190
Th-The hell is he on about?

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.850
Nonoha, what's this
something-or-other special?

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:58.190
Uh, something I made to celebrate

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.690
his birthday when we were kids,

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.930
a special sweets of waffles topped with

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:06.820
pickled radish, filled with kelp tea cream.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:07.670
Blgh!

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.870
It's everything Kaito likes.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.940
It tasted terrible,

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.170
and Kaito called it everything from

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.460
The Worst in History to Hazardous Materials.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.210
Why would he mention that now?

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.770
Hazardous materials?

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:22.220
Hazardous materials could mean...

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.720
Poison, strong medicines... Explosives.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.250
Explosives!

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.790
You go complainin' NOW?

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.450
Kaito Daimon!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.890
This puzzle is so hard,

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.730
it's knocked you
off your high horse, huh?

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:53.030
Yup. Smacked me right off my base!

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.010
Smack... Base?

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:58.220
Ah. So that's it, huh?

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.090
Yes, it looks like it.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.420
That's it!

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.590
Uh, what's what?!

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:11.930
Can you do it, Cubik?

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:12.960
Of course.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:13.640
Ana.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.380
Okay. Here.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.400
And this, right?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.960
What are you all...?

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.760
What does he think he can do now?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.250
Mercury will soon crumble.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.380
You're finally here, Kaito.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.810
With the next move, it's all over.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.490
Kaito!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.170
Kaito!

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:30.930
Kaito...

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:34.190
It can't be. Kaito...

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.490
Impossible!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.780
K-Kaito!

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.410
Did I become eternal?

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.060
Kaito.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.460
There ain't no eternity.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:39.170
When you're dead, you can't

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:41.330
make puzzles anymore, can ya?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.620
The sun isn't collapsing.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.670
Why?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:52.340
He probably found the
part that was meant to

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.030
collapse and wedged it into place.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.480
Done.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.330
Oh, jeez. Well, we made it.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:03.650
Nonoha!

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:06.400
Throw it!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.330
Quick! At the base of the puzzle!

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.820
The support at the bottom right side!

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.780
Wh-Why?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.330
Nonoha!

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:19.450
Hurry and throw it!

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.960
The Sun won't hold!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:30.050
Darn it! I don't understand!

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.060
Rook!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.020
Kaito!

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:53.000
Rook! I WILL save you!

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:56.530
Kaito!

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.030
Kaito...

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.210
Kaito!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:34.480
Kaito...

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:37.180
I'm alive.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.790
And Rook too, of course.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:49.960
Kaito.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.810
Thank goodness.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.090
He really friggin' solved it.

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:01.750
I don't believe it.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:05.940
To think that one could escape
a puzzle in such a way...

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.830
With both of them alive, to boot.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.030
How were you all able to

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.840
understand Kaito Daimon's intent?

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:17.280
Well, because we're geniuses.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.780
That's right.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.910
You all made me throw a BOMB!

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.540
Now, now.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.830
Thanks to that,
the two of them were saved.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.390
I see.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.940
So this makes a Phi-Brain.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.360
Master Rook!

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:55.440
I'm alive?

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:59.700
I said I'd save you, didn't I?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.650
If the Sun hadn't been
made just like this,

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.490
I wouldn't have been able to solve it.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:16.130
Rook... Why did you design
the Sun like this?

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:17.430
Huh?

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.510
I don't know.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:24.660
I just made it
while thinking of you.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.640
I, Ana, think...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.450
Maybe you've wanted to
see it this whole time.

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.850
Kaito solving this puzzle.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:40.000
I'm making a new wooden
cross puzzle right now.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.080
When it's finished, I'll give it to you.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.120
I'm sorry, Rook.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:52.190
I couldn't keep the
promise I made that day.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:53.630
To always solve puzzles with you.

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:59.150
But... I finally solved it.

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:05.320
That's why you'll make
a new puzzle for me, right?

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:13.010
Huh? What's happening?

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.370
That's strange.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:18.030
I haven't cried once since that day.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:19.640
Rook...

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:21.770
I, Ana, think...

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:24.740
Everything has been
swallowed up by the Armlet.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.780
Happiness, sadness...

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.750
Everything in your heart.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.000
Heart...

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.430
The Armlet!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:48.340
Thank you, Kaito.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.430
You saved me.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.270
I want to make puzzles again.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:56.040
Just for you.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:57.980
New puzzles.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:02.360
So... will you solve them, Kaito?

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:04.260
Rook.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:09.350
Of course I will. No question.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.310
The heck?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:15.860
Dude, you're crying?! Wimp!

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.590
Shut up! Shut your mouth, Bastard!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:21.080
What?! If it wasn't for our help,

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.520
you wouldn't have solved that thing!

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:24.890
Huh?! I've saved YOUR skin,

00:21:24.890 --> 00:21:26.020
so you
better watch that tone of yours!

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:30.600
Let me tell ya somethin'
right here and now...

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:30.600
Time that had stopped for Rook
had begun to move.

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:40.650
The Book of God will burn, Jin.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:45.970
Yuugure nante suki ja nakatta
I didn't like when night fell

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:45.220
It's over. Our task, all of it.

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:51.520
Chotto chiisana uso tsuitari shita
So I told a little lie

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:56.530
Mou sukoshi dake issho ni itakute
I wanted to be with you just a little longer

00:21:56.530 --> 00:22:01.310
Toomawari shiteta
So I took the long way

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:07.110
Ano koro no bokura wa zutto
Back then, the two of us always

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:12.660
Kotae wa hitotsu da to shinjitsuzuketeta ne
Kept believing there was only one answer, didn't we?

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:17.140
Douka kawarazu ni ite
Remain unchanged, somehow

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:22.460
Dakishimetara kowaresou datta
If I held you tight, it seemed you'd fall apart

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:27.730
Dakara sotto ryoute de tsutsunda
So I gently wrapped you in both hands

00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:33.450
Kimi ga kureta chiisa na ketsui o
That small measure of resolve you gave me

00:22:31.890 --> 00:22:33.070
I'm sleepy.

00:22:33.070 --> 00:22:35.600
You've been running around since we left.

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:38.170
Ima tokihanatsu kara
I will release it now

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:38.170
I wonder where he is now...

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:40.750
Arigatou
Thank you

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:39.680
Rook.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:46.720
Kaito. I'm going on a journey.

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:49.220
I may have been enthralled by the Armlet,

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:54.790
Kaerimichi hitori de hoshizora o miageta
On that road home, alone, I looked up at the starry sky

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:51.860
but the things I did remain.

00:22:52.810 --> 00:22:56.370
To rebuild the POG,
I have to make up for my sins.

00:22:54.790 --> 00:23:00.170
Boku wa koko ni iru kara
I'll be right here

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:00.270
I think that first, I'll start with
seeing the outside world.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:04.530
Toki ni omoidashite
So think of me sometimes

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:07.550
I'm a little lonely,
but I'll be all right.

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:09.970
Zutto, zutto tomodachi de iyou
Let's always, always be friends

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:09.080
I'm not alone.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:13.110
Because we... are bound by puzzles.

00:23:09.970 --> 00:23:15.150
Donna toki mo kimi o omotteru yo
I'm always thinking of you

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:20.890
Saa, susumou, furikaeranaide
Well, let's move on, not looking back

00:23:20.020 --> 00:23:21.140
Rook...

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:25.710
Sumiwataru sora, boku ga erabu michi
A clear sky, a path I will choose

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:25.160
Well, well, MISTER Kaito Daimon!

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:31.000
Mata aou ne, yakusoku shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:26.110 --> 00:23:28.970
Today, for sure, you shall
accept my challenge!

00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:34.470
This is the RE-revamped
Takeda Sudoku, Version 100!

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:36.420
Douka kimi wa shiawase de ite ne
Find happiness somehow, all right?

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:36.850
Can you solve it, I wonder?

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:41.880
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I am, the path you gave me

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.980
Kaito Daimon!

00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:46.960
Zutto kokoro no naka
Will forever sparkle

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:49.180
Can I solve it, you say?

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:50.980
Hikaru yo
In my heart

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:53.250
There ain't no puzzle I can't solve!

00:24:03.300 --> 00:24:04.950
It's a duel, Kaito!

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:07.460
If I win, I take the main character spot!

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:09.380
Me, the GREAT Gammon!

00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:11.500
Hmph! I could care less about that,

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.040
but I accept.

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:14.510
Your challenge is gonna backfire!

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:16.210
Perhaps, then,

00:24:16.210 --> 00:24:18.980
I should prepare
a suitable puzzle for you two.

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:22.760
Th-This puzzle! Who are you?

00:24:22.760 --> 00:24:25.530
Next time, "Orpheus Order"

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:27.500
Orpheus Order

00:24:25.530 --> 00:24:27.860
Welcome to the puzzle of judgment.
